  data:  # 337e
    kind: work_item  # 337e
    title: "Closure-discipline guard: behavioral invariants must close on behavioral evidence, not proxy metrics"  # 337e
    status: needs_human_review  # 337e
    priority: 2  # 337e
    parent:  # 337e
    tags:  # 337e
    - closure_discipline  # 337e
    - governance  # 337e
    - tracker_hygiene  # 337e
    isbefore: []  # 337e
    duplicate_of: []  # 337e
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 337e
    pr_ref:  # 337e
    description: "**Proposal (governance — needs human approval before implementation).**\n\n**Problem.** INV-nufob was a false-satisfied: closed 2026-06-01 on a *proxy metric* (\"self-analysis at 0 verdict_enum violations\") plus an *adjacency assumption* (credited the sibling INV-mofih `ClaimVerdict.inconclusive` fix), while its actual behavioral invariant — the verify-claims `--taint-*` loader must error, not silently confirm, on bad input — stayed violated until found during the v6.0.0 step-1 re-verification (fixed in PR #4152). A sibling-closure audit over all 978 resolved items found the proxy-closure *pattern* recurs (3 true pure-proxy closures; INV-nufob the only one that hid a live regression). Root cause: nothing requires that a behavioral-invariant closure cite behavioral evidence; a green internal validator count was accepted as proof the user-facing behavior was fixed. This is the same false-all-clear pathology as META-fimas.\n\n**Proposed guard (3 parts).**\n\n1. **New playbook** `.agent/agent_playbooks_protocols_sops_skills/closure-evidence-discipline-playbook.md`: when resolving (`satisfied`/`done`) a tracker item whose statement describes runtime/user-facing BEHAVIOR (CLI exit codes, stdout/stderr, silently-accept/reject, error/traceback), the resolution rationale MUST cite behavioral evidence — a live repro (command + observed exit code / stderr) or a production-path test — NOT solely an internal validator metric (\"N violations\", \"validator clean\", \"0 X\") or an adjacency claim (\"closed by <sibling>'s fix\"). Re-run the item's OWN filed repro at closure. Proxy metrics may SUPPLEMENT but never SUBSTITUTE for behavioral evidence.\n\n2. **AGENTS.md essentialization** (1–3 sentences) in the Tracker section, adjacent to the existing \"Resolution Rationale\" rule, pointing to the playbook. Register the playbook in `.agent/hooks/_shared/on_transcript_change.py` PLAYBOOKS per the \"Creating a New Playbook\" procedure.\n\n3. **Optional soft-check** `scripts/audit-closure-evidence` (on-demand, NOT a hard CI gate — the detector is heuristic): re-runs the audit detector (a proxy-citing closure entry lacking in-entry behavioral evidence, restricted to behavioral-statement items) over the committed tracker corpus and reports candidates for human-reviewed re-probe. Folds into the existing tracker-hygiene/dedup sweep.\n\n**Detector reference (validated this session).** PROXY signal: `self-analysis at \\d`, `verdict_enum`, `spec_validator`, `validator class`, `validation_report`, `zero violations`, `\\b0 (verdict|enum|schema)`, `\\d+ \\w* violations`. BEHAVIORAL signal: `rc[=: ]\\d`, `exit[ -]?\\d`, `live`, `repro`, `stderr|stdout`, a subcommand invocation (`verify-claims`/`run`/`sketch`/…), a `N/M -> N/M` ratio transition, ``` code block, `static code audit`. Flag = behavioral-statement item whose closure has PROXY but no BEHAVIORAL. NOTE: the first detector pass over-flagged (11) because it required a `hypergumbo` prefix before subcommands; the corrected pass found 3 true cases — keep the corrected regex.\n\n**Files touched (all governance → human approval):** AGENTS.md, `.agent/agent_playbooks_protocols_sops_skills/<new>.md`, `.agent/hooks/_shared/on_transcript_change.py`, and (optional) a new `scripts/audit-closure-evidence`. Per AGENTS.md governance workflow, no PR until approved."  # 337e
    fields: {}  # 337e
- op: discuss  # 0cfd
  at: '2026-06-09T22:05:10Z'  # 0cfd
  by: agent  # 0cfd
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 0cfd
  clock: 2  # 0cfd
  nonce: 0cfd  # 0cfd
  message: "DESIGN DECISIONS (human, 2026-06-09): (1) Enforcement strength = (b) ADVISORY — implement the playbook + AGENTS.md essentialization + the on-demand 'audit-closure-evidence' script run during hygiene sweeps; do NOT add a hard pre-commit/CI gate on 'tracker update --status satisfied' (the detector is heuristic — first pass over-flagged 11 vs corrected 3 — so a hard gate would block legitimate closures on false positives). (2) Scope = FORWARD-ONLY — the rule and script apply to future closures; do NOT trigger a retroactive behavioral re-probe of the existing behavioral satisfied/done corpus (the proxy-closure-shaped subset was already audited this session: 3 true pure-proxy, all benign; INV-nufob was the sole hidden false-close and is fixed). Still gated on human approval before implementation (touches AGENTS.md + .agent/** governance files)."  # 0cfd
